James received an email from Apoorva Suresh, expressing interest in graduate research under his advisement at the School of Marine Science & Policy, focusing on economic impacts of climate change and coastal community resilience. Key details included her academic background in field-level adaptation research and a request to discuss potential advising opportunities via email or Zoom. James identified prompts in Apoorva's email, such as the unclear program specifics, his advising and Graduate Research Assistant (GRA) availability, and the suitability of her research interests. In his response, he clarified that he is not accepting new Ph.D. students or GRAs for the admissions cycle and directed her to relevant self-funded master’s programs. He encouraged her to consider applying if the programs aligned with her goals.
